Package: IntegrityAnalysis
Title: Carlisle-Shafer Monte Carlo Analysis of Baseline Data in Randomized Controlled Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Steven",
           family = "Shafer",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "steven.shafer@stanford.edu",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0289-7793"))
Description: A Shiny application implementing the Carlisle-Shafer Monte Carlo
    analysis of baseline data in randomized controlled trials, used in
    editorial screening for fabricated data. Continuous baseline variables are
    tested by simulating rounded group means under the null hypothesis of
    random sampling; categorical variables by simulated chi-square; per-row
    p-values are combined with Stouffer's method. References: Carlisle 2012,
    Carlisle et al. 2015, Carlisle 2017 (Anaesthesia).
